  <Principles><Principle id="P1" name="Single Responsibility"><Description>Order aggregate root manages the order lifecycle: pending → approved → shipped → completed → cancelled. Each state transition publishes domain events (OrderPlaced, OrderApproved, etc.) for downstream processing.</Description><Rationale>Aggregate root ensures order invariants are maintained across all state transitions.</Rationale></Principle></Principles>
  <Features><Feature id="F1" name="Orders " type="core">Direct Status Mutation: Setting order.Status directly instead of using behavior methods.</Feature></Features>
